00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.270 align:start position:0%
 
thank you so much for being on the  program firstly how was your meeting  with emmanuel macron and are you  satisfied with what he said to you  um  well good morning also we do not say  good morning anymore in ukraine  but yeah it is very important for us now  to give personal uh you know evidence  and what is going on in kiev in kharkiv  in other cities we did have a meeting  with uh macron and we were four members  of parliament and women battalion which  we call ourselves now and also a mayor  of melitopol  uh who was captured and who was uh taken  hostage for six days and then was  exchanged for nine russian soldiers so  he he told his experience in being in  captivity uh how host was he treated  what did they want how he was forced to  resign obviously he did not resign and i  think it was incredibly important for  french people for french politicians and  for the french president to hear and to  hear it from somebody who is not resume  but who's been there two days ago just  there in kiev  as to how successful it was  uh well we will see obviously on the  results um we you know we ukraine is  pretty much done with diplomacy we have  been very straightforward we have been  very direct and i will tell you very  honestly if something that macron  promised he did not deliver  but i hope that he will deliver on every  point that we talked about  and i'm very keen to talk about the  individual stories of what's happening  in ukraine but just firstly on macron um  europe and the eu is of course spending  hundreds of millions of pounds every day  on russian  oil and particularly gas  is that acceptable  no it's not acceptable and actually that  question was raised obviously with  president macron and he said that yes  they are ready to do an embargo on  russian oil and gas  they have denied paying in rubles  for it as you know uh as did a lot of  other members of the european union and  we asked macron specifically as a  president or right now as he is the  president of france's presidency in  europe to work with other countries uh  and to work on the unity basically  because if the europe will not be united  then putin will for sure become stronger  and stronger and we do need to stop the  putin together today and together uh  that is why it was very important to  talk to france after actually our visit  to great britain as you may know  just to clarify president macron told  you that he was prepared to do an  embargo on russian  oil and gas  he said that he's prepared yes to go  through if would be needed yes  and do you believe him do you believe  his assurance  um well yesterday we were also you know  at the manifestation because ukrainians  and french people gather in paris in the  plaza de la republique every saturday  for the manifestations to actually put a  pressure on french politicians to stop  buying russian gas to stop buying  russian oil uh to stop putting russian  cargo ships uh to the french ports  uh and and basically to force the  companies which are french companies to  go outside of russia and i think that  this pressure is the main important  pressure why it will work so i'm sure  that actually those manifestations those  meetings um those hundreds of thousands  of people that go every saturday they  are the ones who actually will force it  through till the end  and this is why i am much more  optimistic  you are mentioned there that you were  joined by the mayor who was captured by  russian forces i think many of us will  remember  that story of them taking the mayor and  what exactly did happen to him and how  was he treated  oh  it's obviously better to ask him but  yeah his story is incredible because  well basically he he had the possibility  to communicate was the one who captured  him right so he had the possibility to  ask some questions and to get the  answers because he was there for a while  basically what they wanted from him they  wanted him to resign uh or to  collaborate with them or to appoint a  deputy mayor that would be from the  russian soldier's side and obviously he  did not do that um as far as i  understand they were too scared to  actually kill him or torture him because  his case got to the very highest level  and putting knew about his case  personally  but he's saying that he was asking them  all the time why did you come to my city  and why do you want to do that and the  answers he got were  well incredible from the russian  propaganda side because they would say  that you know  we want to liberate you from the nazi  regime and he was like well i'm 33 years  old i have never seen one nothing in  ukraine what else and they would say  well we know that you uh kill and bully  veterans of the second world war on the  streets and he would be like well there  are 34 veterans alive of the second  world war in my city milital and i am in  constant contact with them and bring  them food you know and then and medicine  and anything they need so this kind of  propaganda talks who have been going for  days and he was trying to as i  understand  well convince them on something but it  was it was an incredible thing how the  russian soldiers at the time were you  know propaganda brainwashed and what did  they think would happen  you say that they were too scared to  kill him or to torture or harm him  of course that is not something that is  afforded to so many of the ukrainian  civilians and this morning we've seen  what has been left after russian forces  retreated from areas around kiev  can you just explain to our viewers the  kind of things that people of ukraine  are witnessing  um well right now unfortunately we have  another city which has been uh destroyed  as mario paul was it's called izum uh in  translation from ukraine from ukrainian  it's raisin so it's supposed to be  something you know  nice and and and and  well and food-like but there is no food  right now in in raisin or in zoom uh  it's been destroyed by 80 percent uh i  think it's becoming the next mario ball  which is a horrifying news for us to  hear it's also in the east of ukraine  there is no food  people have been forced well to stay  underground without food and water as  mario paul were people are not being  able to escape  and basically this humanitarian  catastrophe is that putin is putting on  ukraine continues  we actually did raise a number of  questions  about the international red cross  because you know that the presence of  international red cross was not there on  the ground in those horrible situations  to help people  uh we want either red cross to be much  more present either we want to recross  to make a statement why they are not  present because personally in personal  conversations they say that russia is  not allowing them to be present and is  not accepting their diplomatic immunity  but they are not making a public  statement about that and this is  something which is horribly wrong with  international law and with international  order  so i really hope that international red  cross would go more public  and would be much more helpful for the  people who are there who are in the  worst possible situation right now in  the middle of europe three hours from us  right now  not having food not having water not  knowing whether they would be alive  tomorrow  living in horrible in in absolutely  horrible conditions of fear pain no  medicine nothing delivered and not being  able to go you know to another city in  ukraine and this is something which is  shocking for me even on the 39 days of  war i still i still don't get how did we  allow this to happen  it's horrific situation people just as  you say trapped with no food no water  in the worst possible situation thank  you so much for coming on the program we  value your voice and thank you  thank you thank you

